<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Statute of Autonomy of Catalonia of 1932</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1932">1932</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Statute of Núria</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Statute of Autonomy of Catalonia of 1932 was the law of the Second Spanish Republic that gave Catalonia self-government under the restored Generalitat, with its own parliament and powers over education, culture, public order and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/civil-law">civil law</a>. It was suspended after the revolt of October 1934, restored in 1936 and abolished by Franco in 1938.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/statute-of-autonomy-of-catalonia-1932.jpg" alt="Statute of Autonomy of Catalonia of 1932" width="320" height="450" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Estatuto_de_Nuria.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
